            <div xml:id="d472">

                <pb facs="0820" n="692" sameAs="frus:frus1928v01/pg692"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">724.3415/268: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in Bolivia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Kaufman</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-12-14T16:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">December 14,
                                1928—4 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>36. Your telegram No. 61, December 14, noon. Since the Conference today by
                    unanimous action (except Bolivia which was not present and Paraguay which
                    refrained from voting) offered its good offices, and since I am Chairman of the
                    Conference, I do not <pb facs="0821" n="693" xml:id="pg693"/> desire to suggest
                    anything which might interfere with the action of the Conference or the
                    acceptance of its good offices which I am exceedingly anxious to have Bolivia
                    give.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
